## 4. Where Clinical Communication Lives in the Competency Framework

### 4.1 Internal Medicine ICS1: The Anchor Subcompetency

Clinical communication behaviors map across multiple competency domains but have their primary home in:

- **Interpersonal & Communication Skills (ICS)**: The direct domain for communication behaviors.
- **Professionalism**: Humanism, sensitivity, respectful partnerships.
- **Patient Care & Procedural Skills**: Patient-centered decision-making, treatment adherence, and safety outcomes.

Within the Internal Medicine Milestones, **ICS1 (Patient- and Family-Centered Communication)** serves as the anchor subcompetency, explicitly including shared decision-making, mitigation of communication barriers, agenda-setting, verifying understanding, eliciting values/goals/preferences, and reflecting on bias.

### 4.2 ICS1 Developmental Levels (L1–L5)

| Level | Description | Key Behavioral Descriptors |
|---|---|---|
| **Level 1** | Foundational | Respect and rapport basics; fundamental communication courtesies |
| **Level 2** | Developing | Establishes and maintains a therapeutic relationship in straightforward encounters |
| **Level 3** | Proficient | Therapeutic relationship in challenging encounters; identifies complex communication barriers |
| **Level 4** | Advanced | **Shared decision-making regardless of complexity; mitigates communication barriers** |
| **Level 5** | Expert/Aspirational | Coaches others in communication skills; models barrier mitigation for peers and learners |

The ACGME-I Internal Medicine Milestones (v2.0) provides even more behavior-granular descriptors: setting the agenda, verifying understanding, eliciting values/goals/preferences, reflecting on bias, and using shared decision-making to align patient preferences to clinical options.

**Sources**:
- [US IM Milestones v2.1 (PDF)](https://www.acgme.org/globalassets/pdfs/milestones/internalmedicinemilestones.pdf)
- [ACGME-I IM Milestones v2.0 (PDF)](https://www.acgme-i.org/globalassets/acgme-international/milestones-2.0/internalmedicinemilestones2.0int.pdf)

