## 6. Mapping Observable Behaviors to Competencies and Milestones

This mapping table is the **central reference artifact** connecting transcript-visible behaviors (the NLP pipeline's detection targets) through the label ontology to competency domains and Milestones language.

| Observable Behavior in Transcripts | Framework Tag(s) | Primary ABMS/ACGME Competency Domain | IM ICS1 Milestones Anchor |
|---|---|---|---|
| Sets agenda at start; confirms concern list | `cc_agenda_set` | Interpersonal & Communication Skills | ACGME-I ICS1: "setting the agenda" and "verifying understanding" |
| Uses respectful language / rapport-building | `cc_opening` | ICS; Professionalism | US IM ICS1 Level 1: respect/rapport |
| Supports patient narrative with active listening | `cc_patient_narrative_supported` | ICS | CCG Phase II; foundational to all higher-level behaviors |
| Provides signposting for encounter structure | `cc_structure_signposting` | ICS | CCG Phase III; structural clarity |
| Names emotion ("It sounds like you're worried.") | `nurse_name` | Professionalism; ICS | Supports therapeutic relationship; addresses emotion barriers |
| Shows understanding / validation | `nurse_understand` | Professionalism; ICS | "Establishes and maintains a therapeutic relationship" (ICS1 L2–L3) |
| Expresses respect for patient coping/resilience | `nurse_respect` | Professionalism; ICS | Therapeutic relationship maintenance |
| Offers support / partnership | `nurse_support` | Professionalism; ICS | Barrier mitigation and trust building for complex SDM |
| Explores emotions with open-ended questions | `nurse_explore` | ICS | Deepening understanding to inform care decisions |
| Elicits values/preferences/goals | `sh_assess_values_preferences` | Patient Care; ICS | ACGME-I ICS1: "eliciting values/goals/preferences" |
| Compares options with risks/benefits | `sh_help_compare_options` | Patient Care; ICS | US IM ICS1 Level 4: "shared decision making" |
| Reaches collaborative decision | `sh_reach_decision` | Patient Care; ICS | L4 SDM behaviors |
| Summarizes and checks back (teach-back) | `cc_summary_checkback` | ICS | ACGME-I ICS1: verifying understanding and aligning plans |
| Closes with next steps and safety-netting | `cc_closing_next_steps` | Patient Care; ICS | Patient-centered plan and barrier mitigation; ICS1 higher-level proficiency |
| Ensures privacy/setting for bad news | `sp_setting` | Professionalism; ICS | Environmental and contextual competence |
| Assesses patient's prior knowledge | `sp_perception` | ICS | Patient-centered information delivery |
| Uses plain language for difficult information | `sp_knowledge_plain` | ICS | Health literacy management |
| Addresses emotional reactions to bad news | `sp_emotion_addressed` | Professionalism; ICS | NURSE integration within SPIKES |
| Confirms understanding via teach-back | `ml_teachback_confirm` | ICS | Closing the loop; McLaughlin Step 6 |
| Demonstrates diagnostic parsimony | `cr_diagnostic_parsimony` | Medical Knowledge; Patient Care | Clinical reasoning quality |
| Applies evidence-based exam maneuvers | `exam_targeted_vs_shotgun` | Patient Care | Exam quality over quantity |

**Internal validation**: The SharePoint labeling document (`Labelling_BehaviorAnalysis.docx`) confirms this combined label space and mentions ABMS/ACGME alignment fields.

